  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "XUNPU FPC-05FB-24PH20, 24-pin 0.5mm FPC, H2.0 rear-flip, dual (top+bottom) contact, LCSC C2856831. SMT contact tails / pad row are at the REAR (actuator) face; the mouth / cable entry is on the FAR side (+y local), 4.95mm from the pad centers (datasheets/XUNPU_FPC-05FB-NPH20.pdf + STEP FACE-VERTEX measurement, corrected 2026-07-20 in out/j3-land/ section 7: feet 0.45mm inside the rear wall, mouth slot lips 4.95mm away; body 15.5 x 5.4mm). The earlier 6.55mm figure came from bounding-boxing raw CARTESIAN_POINTs, which picks up LINE / AXIS2_PLACEMENT_3D parameterisation origins at Y-6.802/-8.193 that ZERO VERTEX_POINTs reference -- the real face-vertex bbox is Y[-5.150,+0.250]. Land per the XUNPU drawing: pads 0.3x1.2 @0.5mm at y-1.625, anchor tabs 2.0x1.8 at +/-7.3/+1.625. Pads are numbered so pad 1 = panel circuit 1 and sits NORTH when placed rot 90 (contact tails WEST, mouth EAST toward the board edge; matches DESPI-C02 P1 mating orientation). NOTE: J4 keeps its committed placement, so the true mouth now sits ~1.65mm inboard of the east board edge rather than flush -- functionally fine for an FPC (the cable simply inserts deeper).")
  (tags "FPC FFC XUNPU 24 0.5mm dual-contact")
